+/// edges (`rgdxaCenter`, the widths Word shows), so an auto-fit table keeps its columns instead
+/// of shrinking to its text. Only for a row with the table's columns (`grid`), one cell each, so
+/// no width can disagree with the grid.
+fn size_from_edges(row: &mut Row, edges: &[f32], grid: &[f32]) {
